Fixed. When a --context-strategy checkpoint stop fires, auto-continue no longer runs past it. That covers the REPL and piped mode with --continue-on-silence. Committed as 2cf36d32 ("Fixes #1161"). The REPL part is checked by unit tests only: I didn't watch it happen in a live REPL session.

What was wrong: the user picks checkpoint mode to get a stop-and-restart instead of compaction. But the REPL's auto-continue (on by default) would send "Continue with the remaining work…" right after the checkpoint line. The next turn then compacted at the same 70% threshold, so the setting the user chose was silently replaced by the default they had turned off.

Changes:
• `src/repl.rs`: a new small check, auto_continue_allowed, now decides whether a turn may be continued.
  • The checkpoint flag is reset before each user prompt. Only the -p and piped exit-code paths read it, not the REPL.
  • The flag is checked before every continuation, so a stop that happens during a continued turn is caught too.
  • When it blocks a continue the turn wanted, the REPL prints one dim line: auto-continue skipped: the checkpoint stop asked for a restart, not more turns.
  • I moved the session-time-budget check ahead of this check, so the note never shows for a loop that was going to stop anyway.
• `src/main.rs`: piped_should_continue takes a new checkpoint_stopped argument and goes through the same check. There the flag stays set for the whole process, which is right because a piped run is a single run. The existing tests in main_tests.rs now pass false for it.
• Tests (`src/checkpoint_stop_tests.rs`):
  • One test runs a real checkpoint-stopped prompt and confirms that, without the new check, auto-continue would have continued it. That shows the blocking tests aren't passing for nothing.
  • Other rows: the REPL is blocked even when the turn looks unfinished and work is queued; behaviour is unchanged when there's no stop; piped mode refuses to continue after a stop.
  • I also broke the new check on purpose (with a NEUTERED marker), saw the three new tests fail by name, then restored it and saw them pass. No marker is left in the tree.
• Docs: docs/src/usage/repl.md and docs/src/features/context.md now say a checkpoint stop is never auto-continued.
• `tests/module_size.rs`: the repl.rs size limit went from 3388 to 3411 lines. The file was already at 3391 before this change.

Checks: build, cargo test, cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings and cargo fmt -- --check all pass. I also posted the decision and its reason as the first lines of a comment on #1161.

Piped mode doesn't print the "skipped" line; only the REPL does. The existing checkpoint message and the exit code 2 already show that the run stopped there.
